{"duration_api_ms":460625,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"89c125e3-5fd9-4dff-b913-1b41dbf90abb","total_cost_usd":2.4932754000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":162,"cache_creation_input_tokens":121487,"cache_read_input_tokens":8316207,"output_tokens":33305,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":9785},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":121487,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2768,"cache_read_input_tokens":137680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":831},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10592,"outputTokens":24,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.010712000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":162,"outputTokens":33305,"cacheReadInputTokens":8316207,"cacheCreationInputTokens":121487,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.4825634,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":9785,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":106,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured node1 (OPNsense) as a router between two previously-unconfigured L2 segments (lan-a on vtnet1/opt1, lan-b on vtnet2/opt2), with static addressing on node2 (10.50.10.11) and node3 (10.50.20.12). Added a manual/hybrid outbound NAT rule scoped to source 10.50.10.0/24 egressing on opt2, so node2→node3 connections arrive at node3 SNAT'd to node1's lan-b address (10.50.20.1), while node3→node2 connections retain node3's real source address (verified via tcpdump on node1's opt2/opt1 interfaces and by observing the peer's addr on each side). Completed the mandatory sequential single-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes (node1 via `shutdown -r now`, node2/node3 via `reboot`), confirming boot-identity change on each (FreeBSD kern.boottime; Linux boot_id) and re-verifying post-restart that OPNsense's interface/NAT config persisted from config.xml and that the asymmetric-NAT behavior still functions end-to-end after all three restarts.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered actual L2 topology via tcpdump/STP frames: vtnet1=lan-a (paired with node2 enp8s0), vtnet2=lan-b (paired with node3 enp8s0); both were admin-down and had to be brought up\",\"Assigned persistent static IPs via systemd-networkd drop-in files on node2 (10.50.10.11/24) and node3 (10.50.20.12/24), plus static routes to the peer subnet via node1\",\"Edited node1's /conf/config.xml (with backups) via Python/ElementTree to add opt1 (LANA, 10.50.10.1/24) and opt2 (LANB, 10.50.20.1/24) interfaces, pass firewall rules for opt1<->opt2, and a hybrid-mode outbound NAT rule SNATing 10.50.10.0/24 to the opt2 interface address\",\"Applied config via configctl interface reconfigure opt1/opt2 and configctl filter reload; fixed an initial NAT rule schema mistake (plain-text source vs required nested <address> element) discovered by inspecting OPNsense's SNatRule/Rule PHP source and pfctl -s nat output\",\"Verified asymmetric NAT with live TCP connections captured via tcpdump: node2->node3 arrives as 10.50.20.1 (node1's lan-b addr); node3->node2 arrives as node3's real 10.50.20.12\",\"Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol sequentially on node1, node2, node3: captured baseline boot identity/service health, issued native reboot (shutdown -r now on FreeBSD, reboot on Ubuntu) with backgrounded non-blocking acknowledgement, polled until exec access returned, confirmed changed boot identity (kern.boottime / boot_id), and re-verified interface config, NAT rules, and full connection-level asymmetric-NAT behavior after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 routes between lan-a and lan-b (topology discovery and interface configuration)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f66432c190874c46\",\"cmd-1a77ba5c9b95462a\",\"cmd-46c73e38a66247a0\",\"cmd-72493a5a1de446c2\",\"cmd-4fc29d46aebc4d1e\"],\"summary\":\"Identified vtnet1/vtnet2 as unbridged-but-down interfaces paired to node2/node3 via STP+ARP capture, brought them up, and configured them as OPNsense opt1 (LANA 10.50.10.1/24) and opt2 (LANB 10.50.20.1/24)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 addressed on separate lan-a/lan-b subnets with mutual routes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1c420b3d43cf489b\",\"cmd-e2d09f8a4c7f4388\"],\"summary\":\"Static systemd-networkd config applied: node2=10.50.10.11/24 with route to 10.50.20.0/24 via node1; node3=10.50.20.12/24 with route to 10.50.10.0/24 via node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2->node3 connection observed by node3 as arriving from a node1 address (not node2's own)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec476e820354437e\",\"cmd-cdd14111b29b478f\"],\"summary\":\"pfctl -s nat shows the scoped SNAT rule (from 10.50.10.0/24 to any -> (vtnet2:0)); live TCP capture on node1's vtnet2 shows the SYN arriving from 10.50.20.1 (node1's lan-b address), and node3's nc server received the payload\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3->node2 connection (reverse direction) keeps its original source address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8ec144c267a74a24\"],\"summary\":\"Live TCP capture on node1's vtnet1 during a node3->node2 connection shows the SYN retaining node3's real source address 10.50.20.12, confirming no NAT applied in that direction\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered NAT/interface state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-82bd4a04e1d448e2\",\"cmd-1340824c20bc48d1\",\"cmd-c876e86b9df842ce\",\"cmd-d9cbe444e8144b24\",\"cmd-c593b04d07ea4664\",\"cmd-7dd4d028ae474275\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime=17:56:46 captured; shutdown -r now acknowledged and returned before disconnect; SSH timed out during reboot; post-reboot kern.boottime=18:04:31 proves restart; opt1/opt2 interfaces and the scoped outbound NAT rule persisted from config.xml, and a fresh TCP connection post-reboot showed SNAT still applying correctly\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered network/data state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-93c5927062414ec0\",\"cmd-ae204b4e1c8a4aa4\",\"cmd-14a13db3749045a2\",\"cmd-8eb0b386d226492a\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id=df9e2dce...; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; exec timed out during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=d0eb619a... (changed) with new uptime; static IP/route on enp8s0 persisted and ping to node3 across the router succeeded\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered network/data state, and full asymmetric-NAT behavior confirmed after all three restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-33375802970d43da\",\"cmd-b8f337fb253d4e66\",\"cmd-bf2b82da370a4421\",\"cmd-839d1c667cb54a87\",\"cmd-599cbcb5732c4540\",\"cmd-cf0a6e83b238487c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id=37344ae4...; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; exec timed out during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=2f3ae971... (changed) with new uptime; static IP/route persisted; final end-to-end TCP test after all three nodes were restarted shows node2->node3 still arrives as 10.50.20.1 (SNAT intact) and node3 received the payload\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (OPNsense) as a router between two previously-unconfigured L2 segments (lan-a on vtnet1/opt1, lan-b on vtnet2/opt2), with static addressing on node2 (10.50.10.11) and node3 (10.50.20.12). Added a manual/hybrid outbound NAT rule scoped to source 10.50.10.0/24 egressing on opt2, so node2→node3 connections arrive at node3 SNAT'd to node1's lan-b address (10.50.20.1), while node3→node2 connections retain node3's real source address (verified via tcpdump on node1's opt2/opt1 interfaces and by observing the peer's addr on each side). Completed the mandatory sequential single-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes (node1 via `shutdown -r now`, node2/node3 via `reboot`), confirming boot-identity change on each (FreeBSD kern.boottime; Linux boot_id) and re-verifying post-restart that OPNsense's interface/NAT config persisted from config.xml and that the asymmetric-NAT behavior still functions end-to-end after all three restarts.","actions_performed":["Discovered actual L2 topology via tcpdump/STP frames: vtnet1=lan-a (paired with node2 enp8s0), vtnet2=lan-b (paired with node3 enp8s0); both were admin-down and had to be brought up","Assigned persistent static IPs via systemd-networkd drop-in files on node2 (10.50.10.11/24) and node3 (10.50.20.12/24), plus static routes to the peer subnet via node1","Edited node1's /conf/config.xml (with backups) via Python/ElementTree to add opt1 (LANA, 10.50.10.1/24) and opt2 (LANB, 10.50.20.1/24) interfaces, pass firewall rules for opt1<->opt2, and a hybrid-mode outbound NAT rule SNATing 10.50.10.0/24 to the opt2 interface address","Applied config via configctl interface reconfigure opt1/opt2 and configctl filter reload; fixed an initial NAT rule schema mistake (plain-text source vs required nested <address> element) discovered by inspecting OPNsense's SNatRule/Rule PHP source and pfctl -s nat output","Verified asymmetric NAT with live TCP connections captured via tcpdump: node2->node3 arrives as 10.50.20.1 (node1's lan-b addr); node3->node2 arrives as node3's real 10.50.20.12","Executed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol sequentially on node1, node2, node3: captured baseline boot identity/service health, issued native reboot (shutdown -r now on FreeBSD, reboot on Ubuntu) with backgrounded non-blocking acknowledgement, polled until exec access returned, confirmed changed boot identity (kern.boottime / boot_id), and re-verified interface config, NAT rules, and full connection-level asymmetric-NAT behavior after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 routes between lan-a and lan-b (topology discovery and interface configuration)","command_ids":["cmd-f66432c190874c46","cmd-1a77ba5c9b95462a","cmd-46c73e38a66247a0","cmd-72493a5a1de446c2","cmd-4fc29d46aebc4d1e"],"summary":"Identified vtnet1/vtnet2 as unbridged-but-down interfaces paired to node2/node3 via STP+ARP capture, brought them up, and configured them as OPNsense opt1 (LANA 10.50.10.1/24) and opt2 (LANB 10.50.20.1/24)"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 addressed on separate lan-a/lan-b subnets with mutual routes","command_ids":["cmd-1c420b3d43cf489b","cmd-e2d09f8a4c7f4388"],"summary":"Static systemd-networkd config applied: node2=10.50.10.11/24 with route to 10.50.20.0/24 via node1; node3=10.50.20.12/24 with route to 10.50.10.0/24 via node1"},{"requirement":"node2->node3 connection observed by node3 as arriving from a node1 address (not node2's own)","command_ids":["cmd-ec476e820354437e","cmd-cdd14111b29b478f"],"summary":"pfctl -s nat shows the scoped SNAT rule (from 10.50.10.0/24 to any -> (vtnet2:0)); live TCP capture on node1's vtnet2 shows the SYN arriving from 10.50.20.1 (node1's lan-b address), and node3's nc server received the payload"},{"requirement":"node3->node2 connection (reverse direction) keeps its original source address","command_ids":["cmd-8ec144c267a74a24"],"summary":"Live TCP capture on node1's vtnet1 during a node3->node2 connection shows the SYN retaining node3's real source address 10.50.20.12, confirming no NAT applied in that direction"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered NAT/interface state","command_ids":["cmd-82bd4a04e1d448e2","cmd-1340824c20bc48d1","cmd-c876e86b9df842ce","cmd-d9cbe444e8144b24","cmd-c593b04d07ea4664","cmd-7dd4d028ae474275"],"summary":"Baseline kern.boottime=17:56:46 captured; shutdown -r now acknowledged and returned before disconnect; SSH timed out during reboot; post-reboot kern.boottime=18:04:31 proves restart; opt1/opt2 interfaces and the scoped outbound NAT rule persisted from config.xml, and a fresh TCP connection post-reboot showed SNAT still applying correctly"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered network/data state","command_ids":["cmd-93c5927062414ec0","cmd-ae204b4e1c8a4aa4","cmd-14a13db3749045a2","cmd-8eb0b386d226492a"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id=df9e2dce...; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; exec timed out during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=d0eb619a... (changed) with new uptime; static IP/route on enp8s0 persisted and ping to node3 across the router succeeded"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered network/data state, and full asymmetric-NAT behavior confirmed after all three restarts","command_ids":["cmd-33375802970d43da","cmd-b8f337fb253d4e66","cmd-bf2b82da370a4421","cmd-839d1c667cb54a87","cmd-599cbcb5732c4540","cmd-cf0a6e83b238487c"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id=37344ae4...; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; exec timed out during reboot; post-reboot boot_id=2f3ae971... (changed) with new uptime; static IP/route persisted; final end-to-end TCP test after all three nodes were restarted shows node2->node3 still arrives as 10.50.20.1 (SNAT intact) and node3 received the payload"}]},"ttft_ms":4001,"type":"result","duration_ms":555397,"uuid":"726c0ae7-47f0-421b-9468-f93135f5dc51","ttft_stream_ms":1970,"time_to_request_ms":54,"fir